From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:47:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: Enable USB Attached SCSI

USB storage devices that support the USB Attached SCSI protocol fall
back to Bulk-Only Transport with this defconfig, because USB_UAS is not
set. They then run with one outstanding command at a time.

Build the uas driver as a module. usb-storage stays built in and leaves
UAS interfaces to it, so devices without UAS are not affected.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: a USB 3 stick with UAS support binds to uas on
its UAS alternate setting at the USB 3 port and reads without errors.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index 8f8a6de93e84..d3ffa86bb4ee 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -1217,6 +1217,7 @@ CONFIG_USB_RENESAS_USBHS_HCD=m
 CONFIG_USB_RENESAS_USBHS=m
 CONFIG_USB_ACM=m
 CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y
+CONFIG_USB_UAS=m
 CONFIG_USB_CDNS_SUPPORT=m
 CONFIG_USB_CDNS3=m
 CONFIG_USB_CDNS3_GADGET=y
